  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark cyber-defense art direction, disciplined red/cyan/yellow palette, clear desktop headline, and cohesive bordered panels. Below desktop, polish drops: dense mono labels and body copy become extremely small, the mobile chart is barely legible, long mutation strings wrap awkwardly, and the vaccination cards create a repetitive vertical wall. Tablet spacing also leaves the arena composition feeling stretched, while the mobile/tablet header visibly truncates navigation behind a vague “MORE” affordance. Contrast verification is incomplete for 13 mobile and 3 tablet header nodes, so readability cannot earn a pass by assumption.",
    "fix": "Raise small-text sizes and contrast, simplify mobile labels/content, give the chart more vertical room, and redesign the vaccination sequence as a compact responsive stepper. Make hidden header navigation explicit and verify contrast across tablet/mobile states.",
